<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells 30,000/T May fuel oil at above $98/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells 30,000/T May fuel oil at above $98/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has sold by tender a 30,000-tonne cargo of 3.0-percent fuel oil at above $98 per tonne, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The high sulphur cargo is for delivery May 16-25 free-on-board (fob) from the southern port of Kaohsiung, the official said.</p>
<p>In its last fuel oil export tender, CPC sold more than one 30,000-tonne cargoes of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil at below $100 per tonne, fob, for delivery April 8-26.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3571)</p>
